<title>UK: Nigeria cuts July crude prices by up to 19 cts.</title>
<headline>Nigeria cuts July crude prices by up to 19 cts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian National Petroleum Corp (NNPC) reduced crude contract formula prices for July by between one and 19 cents a barrel from June, traders said.</p>
<p>Following are new prices for July versus benchmark Dated Brent:</p>
<p>		    July	  June	 change</p>
<p>Bonny Light    +26 cts     +42 cts   dn 16 cts</p>
<p>Qua Iboe	 +26 cts     +42 cts   dn 16 cts</p>
<p>Forcados	 +10 cts     +11 cts   dn  1 ct</p>
<p>Escravos	 +19 cts     +34 cts   dn 15 cts</p>
<p>Brass River    +31 cts     +50 cts   dn 19 cts</p>
<p>Pennington     +56 cts     +75 cts   dn 19 cts</p>
<p>Bonny Medium   parity	-1 ct     dn  1 ct</p>
<p>NNPC raised by five cents the cost of its option to price crude one week ahead of bill of lading to a premium of 10 cents.</p>
<p>An option for deferred pricing 14 days after bill of lading also was raised by five cents to 10 cents a barrel.</p>
<p>-- Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
